*Eg :    Steps for Hello world Program*
1.	 *Create a New Android Project*
•	Open Android Studio → "New Project".
•	Choose "Empty View Activity" and click Next.
•	 *Enter project details:*
o	Name: HelloWorld
o	Save Location: Choose a folder.
o	Language: Java or Kotlin (choose Kotlin if unsure; it's recommended for modern Android apps).
o	Minimum SDK: Choose the lowest API level you want to support (e.g., API 21: Lollipop).
•	Click Finish.
2.	 *Edit the Layout XML*
•	Go  to:
app → res → layout → activity_main.xml
•	Create a textView and a button
  
3.	 *Code the logic in MainActivity .java*

On clicking on button, Helloworld should be displayed.

4.	 *Run the App*
•	Click the Run button 
•	Select a device:
o	Physical device (USB Debugging enabled)
o	or Android Emulator
•	You should see "Hello World!" displayed on the screen.
